<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yamada Nagamasa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1590–1630</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yamada Nagamasa was a Japanese adventurer who settled in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ayutthaya-kingdom">Ayutthaya</a> in the early seventeenth century, led the Japanese community and its volunteer soldiers in the service of the Siamese kings, and won high rank at court. Drawn into the succession struggles that brought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prasat-thong">Prasat Thong</a> to power, he was sent to govern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nakhon-si-thammarat">Nakhon Si Thammarat</a> in the south, where he died in 1630, reportedly poisoned.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/yamada-nagamasa.jpg" alt="Yamada Nagamasa" width="320" height="330" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Yamada-Nagamasa-Portrait-Shizuoka-Sengen-Shrine.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Foreign specialists added firearms and expertise: Portuguese gunners served the kings from the sixteenth century, and a Japanese volunteer corps under <b>Yamada Nagamasa</b> fought for the court in the early seventeenth century.</blockquote><a href="/empire/ayutthaya-kingdom">Ayutthaya Kingdom · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>The kings hired foreign mercenaries, and foreigners, lacking ties within the kingdom, often rose high at court: <b>Yamada Nagamasa</b>’s Japanese served as King Songtham’s royal guard.</blockquote><a href="/societies/ayutthaya">Social Hierarchy of the Ayutthaya Kingdom</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Numazu, in what is now <a href="/countries/japan">Japan</a>. Died in Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya, in what is now <a href="/countries/thailand">Thailand</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=35.1,138.86&amp;year=1616" aria-label="Numazu on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="8068 894 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Yamada Nagamasa"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M8518 1164h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M8518 1164h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=35.1,138.86&amp;year=1616">What was here in 1616? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
